  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 30-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence at normal angle. Layer sequence: HfO2(1), SiO2(2), HfO2(3), SiO2(4), ... ending with SiO2(30) adjacent to substrate. Initialize all 30 layer thicknesses from the vector [58.555, 88.888, 54.609, 89.507, 56.204, 98.173, 64.725, 103.146, 62.059, 90.830, 124.964, 86.427, 56.472, 88.946, 121.912, 93.736, 63.099, 176.938, 178.127, 155.323, 119.593, 177.959, 161.513, 88.070, 163.472, 175.203, 117.158, 175.673, 153.443, 132.308] nm with optimization bounds of ±10 nm from each initial value. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer. Spectral objective: maximize transmittance in 1530-1565 nm band, maximize reflectance in 400-700 nm band with 2.0x weight applied to 400-550 nm sub-band relative to 550-700 nm sub-band. Evaluate at normal incidence, unpolarized or both s and p polarization averaged. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 6 alternating HfO2/SiO2 pairs (12 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 400-700 nm, 1530-1565 nm. soft objectives: high transmission in 1530–1565 nm; high reflection in 400–700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: reflection in 1530–1565 nm; transmission in 400–700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 30.",
